# Lead/orchestrator edit whitelist (consumed by scripts/hooks/Invoke-LeadEditGuard.ps1).
# One glob per line; blank lines and # comments ignored. Presence of this file REPLACES
# the built-in default list, so the defaults are restated below.
#
# This file is COMMITTED policy (hand-authored). Runtime STATE lives under
# .team-process/sessions/ (+ the lane file) and is gitignored.

# --- built-in defaults (orchestration assets the lead authors) ---
.claude/team-process/**
.claude/bindings/**
.claude/agents/**
.claude/commands/**
.claude/skills/**
.claude/*.md
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.team-process/**

# --- team-process enforcement hooks (the framework's own guards) ---
# These hook scripts ARE the team-process enforcement arm; authored as one unit by the
# orchestrator who owns the framework.
scripts/hooks/Format-ProtocolForm.ps1
scripts/hooks/Format-ProtocolForm.Tests.ps1
scripts/hooks/Invoke-ProtocolFormGuard.ps1
scripts/hooks/Invoke-ProtocolFormGuard.Tests.ps1
scripts/hooks/Invoke-LeadEditGuard.ps1
scripts/hooks/Invoke-LeadEditGuard.Tests.ps1
scripts/hooks/Invoke-LaneGuard.ps1
scripts/hooks/Invoke-LaneGuard.Tests.ps1
scripts/hooks/Invoke-TeamModeGuard.ps1
scripts/hooks/Invoke-TeamModeGuard.Tests.ps1

# --- team-process utility scripts (framework tooling the orchestrator runs) ---
# Not hooks — orchestration utilities (e.g. publishing the session decision record to the
# owning issue at ship; rendering the team statusline from session records). Authored +
# owned by the orchestrator as part of the framework.
scripts/team-process/**
scripts/statusline/**

# --- repo-level config the framework touches ---
.gitignore
